---
title: Sequence Diagram — Notification Service (Java Multi-threading Deep Dive)
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant KAFKA as Kafka Consumer<br/>(Main Thread)
    participant POOL as ThreadPoolExecutor<br/>(core=5, max=20)
    participant VT as Virtual Threads<br/>(Java 21)
    participant CF as CompletableFuture<br/>Chain
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant EMAIL as Email Server<br/>(SMTP)
    participant PUSH as Push Notification<br/>Service
    participant DLT as Dead Letter Topic

    Note over KAFKA,DLT: Scenario: Article published → Notify 500 followers

    KAFKA->>KAFKA: Poll: ArticleCreatedEvent<br/>{articleId, authorId, title}
    KAFKA->>DB: SELECT followers WHERE<br/>following_user_id = authorId
    DB-->>KAFKA: 500 follower records

    Note over KAFKA,POOL: Strategy 1: ExecutorService with ThreadPool

    KAFKA->>POOL: submitBatch(500 notifications)
    
    Note right of POOL: ThreadPoolExecutor config:<br/>corePoolSize: 5<br/>maxPoolSize: 20<br/>queueCapacity: 100<br/>keepAliveTime: 60s<br/>rejectedHandler: CallerRunsPolicy

    loop For each batch of 50
        POOL->>POOL: Thread-1: Process notifications[0-49]
        POOL->>POOL: Thread-2: Process notifications[50-99]
        POOL->>POOL: Thread-3: Process notifications[100-149]
        POOL->>POOL: Thread-4: Process notifications[150-199]
        POOL->>POOL: Thread-5: Process notifications[200-249]
    end

    Note over VT,CF: Strategy 2: Virtual Threads (Java 21) for I/O-bound work

    KAFKA->>VT: ExecutorService.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()
    
    Note right of VT: Virtual Threads:<br/>• Lightweight (few KB vs 1MB platform thread)<br/>• Managed by JVM, not OS<br/>• Perfect for I/O blocking<br/>• Can create 1M+ simultaneously<br/>• Carrier thread released during I/O wait

    loop For each of 500 followers
        VT->>VT: VirtualThread-1 → send email[0]
        VT->>VT: VirtualThread-2 → send email[1]
        VT->>VT: VirtualThread-... → ...
        VT->>VT: VirtualThread-500 → send email[499]
        Note right of VT: 500 virtual threads run concurrently!<br/>Each blocks on I/O without<br/>consuming an OS thread
    end

    Note over CF,EMAIL: Strategy 3: CompletableFuture Async Chain

    CF->>CF: Step 1: supplyAsync(() → fetchUserPrefs)
    CF->>DB: Query user notification preferences
    DB-->>CF: {email: true, push: true, inApp: true}

    CF->>CF: Step 2: thenApply(prefs → composeMessage)
    CF->>CF: Build personalized notification

    CF->>CF: Step 3: thenCompose(msg → sendAll)

    par Send in parallel
        CF->>EMAIL: thenApplyAsync(() → sendEmail)
        EMAIL-->>CF: Email sent ✅
    and
        CF->>PUSH: thenApplyAsync(() → sendPush)
        PUSH-->>CF: Push sent ✅
    and
        CF->>DB: thenApplyAsync(() → saveInApp)
        DB-->>CF: In-app saved ✅
    end

    CF->>CF: Step 4: allOf(email, push, inApp).join()
    CF->>CF: Step 5: exceptionally(error → handleFailure)

    Note over CF,DLT: Error Handling

    CF->>CF: If any send fails after 3 retries
    CF->>DLT: Publish to dead-letter-topic<br/>for manual investigation

    Note over KAFKA,DLT: Summary: Threading Approaches Used<br/>1. ThreadPoolExecutor → CPU-bound batch processing<br/>2. Virtual Threads → I/O-bound concurrent sends<br/>3. CompletableFuture → Async pipeline with error handling
